<!-- SKIN settings, applied to whichever skin is LIVE when the profile runs
     (stock Estuary on a fresh box, Estuary POV once the owner installs it -
     both carry show_weatherinfo; POV wires it at skin control 704). These are
     NOT core setting ids: a skin bool lives in the live skin's memory and is
     serialized to addon_data/<skin>/settings.xml by the clean-shutdown flush,
     the same mechanism restore's _apply_skin_settings rides (defect A). So the
     apply sets it live via Skin.SetBool and the restart the flow already asks
     for persists it; writing the file instead would be clobbered by that very
     flush. A box that changes skins later re-runs the profile to set it on the
     new skin, additively, like everything else here.

     Only this add-on parses this file, never Kodi, so comments are fine
     (unlike addon_data documents). Shape mirrors Kodi's own skin-settings
     serialization: <setting id type="bool">true|false</setting>. Value
     measured off the owner's hand-set ts1, 2026-08-31: the top-bar weather. -->
<settings>
    <setting id="show_weatherinfo" type="bool">true</setting>
</settings>
